[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "qg-accepted-main 2.c4"]
[Name "The Chigorin Defence: 2...Nc6"]

2... Nc6 { The Chigorin Defence. It develops and adds to the pressure on d4, but the knight blocks the c-pawn, so Black can never hold d5 with ...c6. }
3. Nf3 { Guards d4 and stops ...e5 for now. }
3... dxc4 { The most common move. It is an Accepted with the knight on c6, and the same simple answer works. }
( 3... Bf5? { Gets the bishop out, but it does nothing for d5, which only the queen guards, and she will be chased when she takes back. }
  4. cxd5 Qxd5
  5. Nc3 Qd6
  6. e4 { The queen has been chased twice, and now the bishop is hit as well. White has the whole centre, and the engine has White more than three pawns ahead. [%cal Ge4f5] [%idea centre-pawns] } )
4. e3 { Clears the way for Bxc4. 4.Nc3 is a little stronger, but this keeps the plan you already know. [%cal Gf1c4] }
4... Bg4 { Pins the knight and adds to the pressure on d4. }
5. Bxc4 e6
6. Nc3 Nf6
7. O-O { Castled, with the pawn back and the centre safe. Next h3 asks the bishop to decide, and then e4 comes. [%idea castle-early] } *
